      "id": "b1.grammar.practice-passive-chocolate",
      "level": "B1",
      "topics": ["grammar"],
      "title": "How chocolate is made",
      "text": "Chocolate is made from cacao beans. The beans are grown in hot countries, like Ghana and Ecuador. First, they are picked by hand and left in the sun for a few days. Then they are sent to factories, where they are cleaned and roasted. Chocolate was first drunk in Mexico more than three thousand years ago, and sugar was added much later in Europe. Today, millions of tons of chocolate are eaten every year, and many new flavors have been invented.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    }
  ],
